# Fixed-width element store rejects an underflowed expression

Verifies `a[0] = a[0] - 2` on an `int8[]` array holding `-127` is rejected
instead of storing the promoted `int16` result `-129`.

>>> source
let a: int8[] = [-127]
a[0] = a[0] - 2
print(a[0])

<<< stdout

<<< stderr
eck: array element `-129` cannot be represented as `int8`

<<< exit
1
